small Altar for Edgar Prado ricardina  arango spends her days alone mourning  the death of her eldest son  [Music]  he was my son he never let me be alone  he always said I want to go and see my  mother those soldiers have more  compassion for an animal  on December 15 the Army showed up  protesters outside ricardina's home  Edgar went out to help a wounded man at  the doorstep and was fatally hit in the  chest his neighbor and friend marikispe  was looking out the window when she says  helicopters flew over them she and her  husband ran to a back room for cover  terrified  I thought it was going to be like those  years ago when there were people dead  here and there I thought we have to  escape we just prayed to God  for Maddie and many in ayakucho the  violent demonstrations brought back  memories of a deadly past  ayakuto was at the heart of Peru's  internal armed conflict in the 1980s and  90s security forces and Shining path  Rebels waged a war that left nearly 70  000 people dead most of them civilians  today lawyers are collecting evidence to  build a case against the soldiers who  opened fire in December as well as those  responsible in the chain of command  on Thursday a lawyer filed a  constitutional complaint in parliament  against President Dina voluarte and some  ministers for the deaths and injuries of  protesters by police and the Armed  Forces many people who lived through the  hours the shootings went on around this  area told us they don't want to speak  about what they witnessed because they  say they're afraid of retaliation  prosecutors set a new unit of Human  Rights prosecutors will investigate the  deaths the government says the  investigations will be respected but  regardina doubts her son's Killers will  be prosecuted  I will never fall they will be free they  will be happy they have done so much  damage they have made so many people cry  will they pay someday  thousands of people disappeared during  the armed conflict of the 80s and 90s  and thousands of cases remain unresolved  regardina fears her son's death will  suffer the same fate Mariana Sanchez
 

